/-!
# Quasicentral approximate units in C⋆-algebras

An ordinary increasing approximate unit of a closed two-sided ideal `I` in a C⋆-algebra `A` need
not commute asymptotically with elements of the ambient algebra: for the compact operators
`K(ℓ²) ⊆ B(ℓ²)`, the finite-rank coordinate projections `P_n` form an increasing approximate unit
of `K(ℓ²)`, yet `‖P_n S - S P_n‖ = 1` for every `n` when `S` is the unilateral shift.

Arveson (1977) and Akemann–Pedersen (1977) proved that every closed two-sided ideal `I` of a
C⋆-algebra `A` nevertheless admits a positive contractive approximate unit along which all
commutators `e * a - a * e` (`a ∈ A`) tend to `0` in norm. Following Akemann–Pedersen and Pedersen
(*C*-Algebras and their Automorphism Groups*, Proposition 3.12.14; see also Davidson, *C*-Algebras
by Example*, Theorem I.9.15), one fixes finite sets `G ⊆ I` and `F ⊆ A` and chooses elements
`u_0, …, u_{n-1} ∈ I` inductively along the canonical increasing approximate unit of `I` so that
each `u_j` nearly fixes the ideal elements `d_i^*` and `d_i^* a` (`d_i = u_i a - a u_i`) on the
right for all `i < j`. Since
`d_i^* d_j = (d_i^* u_j - d_i^*) a - (d_i^* a u_j - d_i^* a)`,
the off-diagonal products `d_i^* d_j` (`i ≠ j`) are uniformly small, whereas the `n` diagonal norms
`‖d_i^* d_i‖ ≤ 4 ‖a‖^2` are damped by `1 / n` in the Cesàro average
`e = n⁻¹ • ∑_{i < n} u_i` via the C⋆-identity estimate
`TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.norm_sum_sq_le`.

## Main declarations

* `TwoSidedIdeal.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit`: predicate that a filter `l : Filter A` is a
  proper filter eventually supported in the nonnegative closed unit ball of `I` along which left
  and right multiplications fix elements of `I` and commutators with elements of `A` tend to `0`.
* `TwoSidedIdeal.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit.of_tendsto_mul_right_of_dense` and
  `of_tendsto_mul_left_of_dense`: check quasicentrality on a subset `sI` whose closure contains `I`
  and a dense subset `sA` of `A`.
* `TwoSidedIdeal.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit.tendstoUniformlyOn_mul_right`,
  `tendstoUniformlyOn_commutator`, `tendstoUniformlyOn_mul_left`: uniform convergence of ideal
  multiplications on compact subsets of `I` and of commutators on arbitrary compact subsets of `A`.
* `TwoSidedIdeal.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit.isIncreasingApproximateUnit_comap_coe` and
  `TwoSidedIdeal.isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_map_coe_iff`: subtype pullback and pushforward
  characterizations between quasicentral approximate units of a closed ideal `I` and
  `Filter.IsIncreasingApproximateUnit` on `I`.
* `TwoSidedIdeal.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit.map`: a surjective `⋆`-algebra homomorphism carries
  a quasicentral approximate unit of `I` to one of `I.map f` (and hence of its closure).
* `TwoSidedIdeal.quasicentralApproximateUnit`: the canonical filter generated by the finite-set
  quasicentral approximation neighborhoods of `I`, characterized by
  `hasBasis_quasicentralApproximateUnit`, `mem_quasicentralApproximateUnit_iff`, and the universal
  property `isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_neBot_and_le`.
* `TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.norm_sum_sq_le`: C⋆-identity bound on the squared norm of a finite sum in a
  C⋆-ring with bounded diagonal norms and off-diagonal products `star (d i) * d j`.
* `TwoSidedIdeal.exists_mem_nonneg_norm_le_one_norm_mul_sub_lt_norm_commutator_lt`,
  `TwoSidedIdeal.quasicentralApproximateUnit_neBot`,
  `TwoSidedIdeal.isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_quasicentralApproximateUnit`, and
  `TwoSidedIdeal.exists_isQuasicentralApproximateUnit`: Arveson's existence theorem for closed
  two-sided ideals.
* `TwoSidedIdeal.exists_isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_exists_seq` and
  `TwoSidedIdeal.exists_seq_isQuasicentralApproximateUnit`: sequential quasicentral approximate
  units when `A` is separable.

## References

* William Arveson, *Notes on extensions of C*-algebras*, Duke Math. J. 44 (1977), 329–355,
  Theorem 1.
* Charles A. Akemann and Gert K. Pedersen, *Ideal perturbations of elements in C*-algebras*,
  Math. Scand. 41 (1977), 117–139, Theorem 3.1.
* Gert K. Pedersen, *C*-Algebras and their Automorphism Groups*, Academic Press, 1979,
  Proposition 3.12.14.
* Bruce Blackadar, *Operator Algebras: Theory of C*-Algebras and von Neumann Algebras*,
  Encyclopaedia of Mathematical Sciences 122, Springer, 2006, §II.4.3.
* Kenneth R. Davidson, *C*-Algebras by Example*, Fields Institute Monographs 6, AMS, 1996,
  Theorem I.9.15.
-/

public section

open Filter Topology
open scoped CStarAlgebra

section Helpers

private theorem norm_commutator_le_two_mul_norm {A : Type*} [NonUnitalSeminormedRing A]
    {e : A} (he : ‖e‖ ≤ 1) (a : A) : ‖e * a - a * e‖ ≤ 2 * ‖a‖ :=
  calc ‖e * a - a * e‖ ≤ ‖e * a‖ + ‖a * e‖ := norm_sub_le _ _
    _ ≤ ‖e‖ * ‖a‖ + ‖a‖ * ‖e‖ := add_le_add (norm_mul_le _ _) (norm_mul_le _ _)
    _ ≤ 1 * ‖a‖ + ‖a‖ * 1 := add_le_add
        (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right he (norm_nonneg a))
        (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left he (norm_nonneg a))
    _ = 2 * ‖a‖ := by ring

private theorem lipschitzWith_mul_right_of_norm_le_one {A : Type*} [NonUnitalSeminormedRing A]
    {e : A} (he : ‖e‖ ≤ 1) : LipschitzWith 1 (e * ·) :=
  LipschitzWith.of_dist_le_mul fun x y => by
    rw [NNReal.coe_one, one_mul, dist_eq_norm, dist_eq_norm, ← mul_sub]
    exact (norm_mul_le _ _).trans (mul_le_of_le_one_left (norm_nonneg _) he)

private theorem lipschitzWith_mul_left_of_norm_le_one {A : Type*} [NonUnitalSeminormedRing A]
    {e : A} (he : ‖e‖ ≤ 1) : LipschitzWith 1 (· * e) :=
  LipschitzWith.of_dist_le_mul fun x y => by
    rw [NNReal.coe_one, one_mul, dist_eq_norm, dist_eq_norm, ← sub_mul]
    exact (norm_mul_le _ _).trans (mul_le_of_le_one_right (norm_nonneg _) he)

private theorem lipschitzWith_commutator_of_norm_le_one {A : Type*} [NonUnitalSeminormedRing A]
    {e : A} (he : ‖e‖ ≤ 1) : LipschitzWith 2 (fun a => e * a - a * e) :=
  LipschitzWith.of_dist_le_mul fun a c => by
    have heq : (e * a - a * e) - (e * c - c * e) = e * (a - c) - (a - c) * e := by noncomm_ring
    rw [NNReal.coe_ofNat, dist_eq_norm, dist_eq_norm, heq]
    exact norm_commutator_le_two_mul_norm he (a - c)

private theorem tendsto_of_mem_closure_of_lipschitzWith {A : Type*} [SeminormedAddCommGroup A]
    {l : Filter A} (hnorm : ∀ᶠ e in l, ‖e‖ ≤ 1) {g : A → A → A} {f : A → A} {L : NNReal}
    (hg : ∀ e : A, ‖e‖ ≤ 1 → LipschitzWith L (g e)) (hf : Continuous f)
    {s : Set A} (hs : ∀ x ∈ s, Tendsto (g · x) l (𝓝 (f x))) {x : A} (hx : x ∈ closure s) :
    Tendsto (g · x) l (𝓝 (f x)) := by
  let B := Metric.closedBall (0 : A) 1
  have hmap : (l.comap ((↑) : B → A)).map ((↑) : B → A) = l :=
    map_comap_of_mem (hnorm.mono fun e he => ⟨⟨e, mem_closedBall_zero_iff.mpr he⟩, rfl⟩)
  have heq : Equicontinuous (fun b : B => g b.1) :=
    (LipschitzWith.uniformEquicontinuous (fun b : B => g b.1) L fun b =>
      hg b.1 (mem_closedBall_zero_iff.mp b.2)).equicontinuous
  have hclosed : IsClosed {y : A | Tendsto (fun b : B => g b.1 y) (l.comap (↑)) (𝓝 (f y))} :=
    heq.isClosed_setOfPred_tendsto hf
  have hmem : x ∈ {y : A | Tendsto (fun b : B => g b.1 y) (l.comap (↑)) (𝓝 (f y))} :=
    closure_minimal (fun y hy => (hs y hy).comp tendsto_comap) hclosed hx
  rwa [← hmap, tendsto_map'_iff]

private theorem tendstoUniformlyOn_of_lipschitzWith {A : Type*} [SeminormedAddCommGroup A]
    {l : Filter A} (hnorm : ∀ᶠ e in l, ‖e‖ ≤ 1) {g : A → A → A} {f : A → A} {L : NNReal}
    (hg : ∀ e : A, ‖e‖ ≤ 1 → LipschitzWith L (g e)) {K : Set A} (hK : IsCompact K)
    (hs : ∀ x ∈ K, Tendsto (g · x) l (𝓝 (f x))) :
    TendstoUniformlyOn g f l K := by
  let B := Metric.closedBall (0 : A) 1
  have hmap : (l.comap ((↑) : B → A)).map ((↑) : B → A) = l :=
    map_comap_of_mem (hnorm.mono fun e he => ⟨⟨e, mem_closedBall_zero_iff.mpr he⟩, rfl⟩)
  have heq : EquicontinuousOn (fun b : B => g b.1) K :=
    (LipschitzWith.uniformEquicontinuous (fun b : B => g b.1) L fun b =>
      hg b.1 (mem_closedBall_zero_iff.mp b.2)).equicontinuous.equicontinuousOn K
  have hunif : TendstoUniformlyOn (fun b : B => g b.1) f (l.comap (↑)) K :=
    heq.tendstoUniformlyOn_of_tendsto hK fun x hx => (hs x hx).comp tendsto_comap
  exact fun u hu => by rw [← hmap, eventually_map]; exact hunif u hu

end Helpers

namespace TwoSidedIdeal

section Basic

variable {A : Type*} [NonUnitalCStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A]

/-- A *quasicentral approximate unit* for a two-sided ideal `I` of a C⋆-algebra `A` is a proper
filter `l` on `A` eventually supported in the nonnegative closed unit ball of `I` such that
`e * x → x` and `x * e → x` for every `x ∈ I`, and `e * a - a * e → 0` for every `a : A`. -/
structure IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) (l : Filter A) : Prop where
  /-- The filter is proper (`l ≠ ⊥`). -/
  protected [neBot : l.NeBot]
  /-- Elements along `l` eventually lie in `I`. -/
  eventually_mem : ∀ᶠ e in l, e ∈ I
  /-- Elements along `l` are eventually nonnegative. -/
  eventually_nonneg : ∀ᶠ e in l, 0 ≤ e
  /-- Elements along `l` are eventually contractions (`‖e‖ ≤ 1`). -/
  eventually_norm : ∀ᶠ e in l, ‖e‖ ≤ 1
  /-- Left multiplication along `l` approximates every element of `I`. -/
  tendsto_mul_right {x : A} (hx : x ∈ I) : Tendsto (· * x) l (𝓝 x)
  /-- Right multiplication along `l` approximates every element of `I`. -/
  tendsto_mul_left {x : A} (hx : x ∈ I) : Tendsto (x * ·) l (𝓝 x)
  /-- Commutators with every element of the ambient algebra `A` tend to `0` along `l`. -/
  tendsto_commutator (a : A) : Tendsto (fun e => e * a - a * e) l (𝓝 0)

/-- Explicit conjunction characterization of `TwoSidedIdeal.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit`. -/
theorem isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff {I : TwoSidedIdeal A} {l : Filter A} :
    I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l ↔
      l.NeBot ∧ (∀ᶠ e in l, e ∈ I ∧ 0 ≤ e ∧ ‖e‖ ≤ 1) ∧
        (∀ x ∈ I, Tendsto (· * x) l (𝓝 x)) ∧
        (∀ x ∈ I, Tendsto (x * ·) l (𝓝 x)) ∧
        (∀ a : A, Tendsto (fun e => e * a - a * e) l (𝓝 0)) := by
  simp only [eventually_and]
  exact ⟨fun h => ⟨h.neBot, ⟨h.eventually_mem, h.eventually_nonneg, h.eventually_norm⟩,
      fun _ hx => h.tendsto_mul_right hx, fun _ hx => h.tendsto_mul_left hx, h.tendsto_commutator⟩,
    fun ⟨hne, ⟨hm, hn, hno⟩, hmr, hml, hc⟩ =>
      { neBot := hne, eventually_mem := hm, eventually_nonneg := hn, eventually_norm := hno,
        tendsto_mul_right := fun hx => hmr _ hx, tendsto_mul_left := fun hx => hml _ hx,
        tendsto_commutator := hc }⟩

namespace IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit

variable {I : TwoSidedIdeal A} {l : Filter A}

/-- Quasicentrality upgrades a left approximate unit of `I` to a two-sided quasicentral
approximate unit, since `x * e = e * x - (e * x - x * e)`. -/
theorem of_tendsto_mul_right [l.NeBot] (hmem : ∀ᶠ e in l, e ∈ I)
    (hnonneg : ∀ᶠ e in l, 0 ≤ e) (hnorm : ∀ᶠ e in l, ‖e‖ ≤ 1)
    (hmul : ∀ x ∈ I, Tendsto (· * x) l (𝓝 x))
    (hcomm : ∀ a : A, Tendsto (fun e => e * a - a * e) l (𝓝 0)) :
    I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l where
  eventually_mem := hmem
  eventually_nonneg := hnonneg
  eventually_norm := hnorm
  tendsto_mul_right hx := hmul _ hx
  tendsto_mul_left {x} hx := by
    simpa only [sub_zero, sub_sub_cancel] using (hmul x hx).sub (hcomm x)
  tendsto_commutator := hcomm

/-- Quasicentrality upgrades a right approximate unit of `I` to a two-sided quasicentral
approximate unit, since `e * x = (e * x - x * e) + x * e`. -/
theorem of_tendsto_mul_left [l.NeBot] (hmem : ∀ᶠ e in l, e ∈ I)
    (hnonneg : ∀ᶠ e in l, 0 ≤ e) (hnorm : ∀ᶠ e in l, ‖e‖ ≤ 1)
    (hmul : ∀ x ∈ I, Tendsto (x * ·) l (𝓝 x))
    (hcomm : ∀ a : A, Tendsto (fun e => e * a - a * e) l (𝓝 0)) :
    I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l where
  eventually_mem := hmem
  eventually_nonneg := hnonneg
  eventually_norm := hnorm
  tendsto_mul_right {x} hx := by
    simpa only [zero_add, sub_add_cancel] using (hcomm x).add (hmul x hx)
  tendsto_mul_left hx := hmul _ hx
  tendsto_commutator := hcomm

/-- Dense-subset criterion for `IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit`: for a proper filter `l` eventually
in the nonnegative closed unit ball of `I`, checking `e * x → x` on a subset `sI` with
`(I : Set A) ⊆ closure sI` and `e * a - a * e → 0` on a dense subset `sA` of `A` suffices for
`I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l`. -/
theorem of_tendsto_mul_right_of_dense [l.NeBot] (hmem : ∀ᶠ e in l, e ∈ I)
    (hnonneg : ∀ᶠ e in l, 0 ≤ e) (hnorm : ∀ᶠ e in l, ‖e‖ ≤ 1)
    {sI sA : Set A} (hsI : (I : Set A) ⊆ closure sI) (hsA : Dense sA)
    (hmul : ∀ x ∈ sI, Tendsto (· * x) l (𝓝 x))
    (hcomm : ∀ a ∈ sA, Tendsto (fun e => e * a - a * e) l (𝓝 0)) :
    I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l :=
  of_tendsto_mul_right hmem hnonneg hnorm
    (fun _ hx => tendsto_of_mem_closure_of_lipschitzWith hnorm
      (fun _ => lipschitzWith_mul_right_of_norm_le_one) continuous_id hmul (hsI hx))
    (fun a => tendsto_of_mem_closure_of_lipschitzWith hnorm
      (fun _ => lipschitzWith_commutator_of_norm_le_one) continuous_const hcomm (hsA a))

/-- Dense-subset criterion for `IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit`: for a proper filter `l` eventually
in the nonnegative closed unit ball of `I`, checking `x * e → x` on a subset `sI` with
`(I : Set A) ⊆ closure sI` and `e * a - a * e → 0` on a dense subset `sA` of `A` suffices for
`I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l`. -/
theorem of_tendsto_mul_left_of_dense [l.NeBot] (hmem : ∀ᶠ e in l, e ∈ I)
    (hnonneg : ∀ᶠ e in l, 0 ≤ e) (hnorm : ∀ᶠ e in l, ‖e‖ ≤ 1)
    {sI sA : Set A} (hsI : (I : Set A) ⊆ closure sI) (hsA : Dense sA)
    (hmul : ∀ x ∈ sI, Tendsto (x * ·) l (𝓝 x))
    (hcomm : ∀ a ∈ sA, Tendsto (fun e => e * a - a * e) l (𝓝 0)) :
    I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l :=
  of_tendsto_mul_left hmem hnonneg hnorm
    (fun _ hx => tendsto_of_mem_closure_of_lipschitzWith hnorm
      (fun _ => lipschitzWith_mul_left_of_norm_le_one) continuous_id hmul (hsI hx))
    (fun a => tendsto_of_mem_closure_of_lipschitzWith hnorm
      (fun _ => lipschitzWith_commutator_of_norm_le_one) continuous_const hcomm (hsA a))

/-- Elements along a quasicentral approximate unit eventually have `nnnorm` at most `1`. -/
theorem eventually_nnNorm (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) : ∀ᶠ e in l, ‖e‖₊ ≤ 1 :=
  hl.eventually_norm

/-- The closed unit ball belongs to any quasicentral approximate unit. -/
theorem closedBall_mem (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) : Metric.closedBall 0 1 ∈ l := by
  simpa [Metric.closedBall] using! hl.eventually_norm

/-- Reversed commutators `a * e - e * a` also tend to `0` along a quasicentral approximate unit. -/
theorem tendsto_commutator_rev (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) (a : A) :
    Tendsto (fun e => a * e - e * a) l (𝓝 0) := by
  simpa only [neg_sub, neg_zero] using (hl.tendsto_commutator a).neg

/-- Every proper subfilter of a quasicentral approximate unit is again a quasicentral approximate
unit (passing to subnets). -/
theorem mono (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) {l' : Filter A} (hle : l' ≤ l) [l'.NeBot] :
    I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l' where
  eventually_mem := hl.eventually_mem.filter_mono hle
  eventually_nonneg := hl.eventually_nonneg.filter_mono hle
  eventually_norm := hl.eventually_norm.filter_mono hle
  tendsto_mul_right hx := (hl.tendsto_mul_right hx).mono_left hle
  tendsto_mul_left hx := (hl.tendsto_mul_left hx).mono_left hle
  tendsto_commutator a := (hl.tendsto_commutator a).mono_left hle

/-- A quasicentral approximate unit for `I` is also a quasicentral approximate unit for its
topological closure `I.topologicalClosure`. -/
theorem topologicalClosure (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) :
    I.topologicalClosure.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l := by
  have := hl.neBot
  exact of_tendsto_mul_right_of_dense
    (hl.eventually_mem.mono fun _ he => I.le_topologicalClosure he)
    hl.eventually_nonneg hl.eventually_norm (sI := I) (sA := Set.univ)
    (fun _ hx => I.mem_topologicalClosure.mp hx) dense_univ
    (fun _ hx => hl.tendsto_mul_right hx) (fun a _ => hl.tendsto_commutator a)

/-- Along a quasicentral approximate unit of `I`, `e * x → x` uniformly on compact subsets of
`I`. -/
theorem tendstoUniformlyOn_mul_right (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) {K : Set A}
    (hK : IsCompact K) (hKI : K ⊆ I) : TendstoUniformlyOn (fun e x => e * x) id l K :=
  tendstoUniformlyOn_of_lipschitzWith hl.eventually_norm
    (fun _ => lipschitzWith_mul_right_of_norm_le_one) hK fun _ hx => hl.tendsto_mul_right (hKI hx)

/-- Along a quasicentral approximate unit, commutators `e * a - a * e` tend to `0` uniformly on
every compact subset `K` of `A`. -/
theorem tendstoUniformlyOn_commutator (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) {K : Set A}
    (hK : IsCompact K) : TendstoUniformlyOn (fun e a => e * a - a * e) 0 l K :=
  tendstoUniformlyOn_of_lipschitzWith hl.eventually_norm
    (fun _ => lipschitzWith_commutator_of_norm_le_one) hK fun a _ => hl.tendsto_commutator a

/-- Along a quasicentral approximate unit of `I`, `x * e → x` uniformly on compact subsets of
`I`. -/
theorem tendstoUniformlyOn_mul_left (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) {K : Set A}
    (hK : IsCompact K) (hKI : K ⊆ I) : TendstoUniformlyOn (fun e x => x * e) id l K := by
  simpa only [Pi.sub_def, id_eq, Pi.zero_apply, sub_zero, sub_sub_cancel] using
    (hl.tendstoUniformlyOn_mul_right hK hKI).sub (hl.tendstoUniformlyOn_commutator hK)

/-- Pulling a quasicentral approximate unit of a closed two-sided ideal `I` back along the subtype
coercion `I → A` produces an increasing approximate unit of the C⋆-algebra `I`. -/
theorem isIncreasingApproximateUnit_comap_coe [IsClosed (I : Set A)]
    (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) :
    (l.comap ((↑) : I → A)).IsIncreasingApproximateUnit where
  neBot := hl.neBot.comap_of_range_mem (hl.eventually_mem.mono fun e he => ⟨⟨e, he⟩, rfl⟩)
  tendsto_mul_left x := by
    rw [IsInducing.subtypeVal.tendsto_nhds_iff]
    exact (hl.tendsto_mul_left x.2).comp tendsto_comap
  tendsto_mul_right x := by
    rw [IsInducing.subtypeVal.tendsto_nhds_iff]
    exact (hl.tendsto_mul_right x.2).comp tendsto_comap
  eventually_nonneg := hl.eventually_nonneg.comap _
  eventually_norm := hl.eventually_norm.comap _

/-- Pushing `l.comap ((↑) : I → A)` forward to `A` recovers `l`. -/
theorem map_coe_comap_coe (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) :
    (l.comap ((↑) : I → A)).map ((↑) : I → A) = l :=
  map_comap_of_mem (hl.eventually_mem.mono fun e he => ⟨⟨e, he⟩, rfl⟩)

/-- Elements along a quasicentral approximate unit in a star-ordered C⋆-algebra are eventually
self-adjoint. -/
theorem eventually_isSelfAdjoint [StarOrderedRing A] (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) :
    ∀ᶠ e in l, IsSelfAdjoint e :=
  hl.eventually_nonneg.mono fun _ => IsSelfAdjoint.of_nonneg

/-- Elements along a quasicentral approximate unit in a star-ordered C⋆-algebra are eventually
fixed by `star`. -/
theorem eventually_star_eq [StarOrderedRing A] (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) :
    ∀ᶠ e in l, star e = e :=
  hl.eventually_isSelfAdjoint.mono fun _ => IsSelfAdjoint.star_eq

end IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit

/-- `pure 0` is a quasicentral approximate unit for the zero ideal `⊥`. -/
theorem IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit.bot_pure_zero :
    (⊥ : TwoSidedIdeal A).IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit (pure 0) where
  eventually_mem := by simp
  eventually_nonneg := by simp
  eventually_norm := by simp
  tendsto_mul_right hx := by
    rw [TwoSidedIdeal.mem_bot] at hx
    subst hx
    simp only [mul_zero]
    exact tendsto_const_nhds
  tendsto_mul_left hx := by
    rw [TwoSidedIdeal.mem_bot] at hx
    subst hx
    simp only [zero_mul]
    exact tendsto_const_nhds
  tendsto_commutator a := by
    simpa only [zero_mul, mul_zero, sub_self] using
      tendsto_pure_nhds (fun e : A => e * a - a * e) 0

/-- The only quasicentral approximate unit for the zero ideal `⊥` is `pure 0`. -/
@[simp]
theorem isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_bot_iff {l : Filter A} :
    (⊥ : TwoSidedIdeal A).IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l ↔ l = pure 0 :=
  ⟨fun hl => hl.neBot.eq_pure_iff.mpr (hl.eventually_mem.mono fun _ h => by simpa using h),
   fun h => h ▸ IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit.bot_pure_zero⟩

/-- A quasicentral approximate unit for `⊤` is an increasing approximate unit of `A` along which
all commutators tend to `0`. -/
theorem isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_top_iff {l : Filter A} :
    (⊤ : TwoSidedIdeal A).IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l ↔
      l.IsIncreasingApproximateUnit ∧ ∀ a : A, Tendsto (fun e => e * a - a * e) l (𝓝 0) :=
  ⟨fun hl => ⟨{ neBot := hl.neBot
                tendsto_mul_left := fun _ => hl.tendsto_mul_left trivial
                tendsto_mul_right := fun _ => hl.tendsto_mul_right trivial
                eventually_nonneg := hl.eventually_nonneg
                eventually_norm := hl.eventually_norm }, hl.tendsto_commutator⟩,
   fun ⟨hl, hc⟩ => { neBot := hl.neBot
                     eventually_mem := Eventually.of_forall fun _ => trivial
                     eventually_nonneg := hl.eventually_nonneg
                     eventually_norm := hl.eventually_norm
                     tendsto_mul_right := fun _ => hl.tendsto_mul_right _
                     tendsto_mul_left := fun _ => hl.tendsto_mul_left _
                     tendsto_commutator := hc }⟩

/-- Pushing a filter `l : Filter I` on a closed two-sided ideal `I` forward to `A` yields a
quasicentral approximate unit of `I` if and only if `l` is an increasing approximate unit of `I`
along which ambient commutators tend to `0`. -/
theorem isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_map_coe_iff {I : TwoSidedIdeal A} [IsClosed (I : Set A)]
    {l : Filter I} :
    I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit (l.map ((↑) : I → A)) ↔
      l.IsIncreasingApproximateUnit ∧
        ∀ a : A, Tendsto (fun e : I => (e : A) * a - a * (e : A)) l (𝓝 0) := by
  refine ⟨fun hl => ⟨?_, fun a => tendsto_map'_iff.mp (hl.tendsto_commutator a)⟩,
    fun ⟨hl, hc⟩ => ?_⟩
  · simpa only [comap_map Subtype.coe_injective] using hl.isIncreasingApproximateUnit_comap_coe
  · have := hl.neBot
    exact .of_tendsto_mul_right
      (eventually_map.mpr (Eventually.of_forall fun e => e.2))
      (eventually_map.mpr hl.eventually_nonneg)
      (eventually_map.mpr hl.eventually_norm)
      (fun x hx => tendsto_map'_iff.mpr <|
        (continuous_subtype_val.tendsto ⟨x, hx⟩).comp (hl.tendsto_mul_right ⟨x, hx⟩))
      (fun a => tendsto_map'_iff.mpr (hc a))

end Basic

/-- In a unital C⋆-algebra, `pure 1` is a quasicentral approximate unit for `⊤`. -/
theorem IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit.top_pure_one {A : Type*} [CStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A]
    [StarOrderedRing A] : (⊤ : TwoSidedIdeal A).IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit (pure 1) :=
  isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_top_iff.mpr
    ⟨.pure_one A, fun a => by
      simpa only [one_mul, mul_one, sub_self] using
        tendsto_pure_nhds (fun e : A => e * a - a * e) 1⟩

/-- In a commutative C⋆-algebra, every increasing approximate unit of a closed two-sided ideal
pushed forward to the ambient algebra is automatically quasicentral. -/
theorem IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit.map_coe_of_isIncreasingApproximateUnit {A : Type*}
    [NonUnitalCommCStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A] {I : TwoSidedIdeal A} [IsClosed (I : Set A)]
    {l : Filter I} (hl : l.IsIncreasingApproximateUnit) :
    I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit (l.map ((↑) : I → A)) :=
  isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_map_coe_iff.mpr ⟨hl, fun a => by
    simp only [mul_comm _ a, sub_self]
    exact tendsto_const_nhds⟩

section Map

variable {A B F : Type*} [NonUnitalCStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]
  [NonUnitalCStarAlgebra B] [PartialOrder B] [StarOrderedRing B]
  [FunLike F A B] [NonUnitalAlgHomClass F ℂ A B] [StarHomClass F A B]

/-- The image of a quasicentral approximate unit of `I` under a surjective `⋆`-algebra homomorphism
`f` is a quasicentral approximate unit of `I.map f`. -/
theorem IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit.map {I : TwoSidedIdeal A} {l : Filter A}
    (hl : I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) (f : F) (hf : Function.Surjective f) :
    (I.map f).IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit (l.map f) := by
  have := hl.neBot
  have hcomm (b : B) : Tendsto (fun e => f e * b - b * f e) l (𝓝 0) := by
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hf b
    simpa only [Function.comp_def, map_sub, map_mul, map_zero] using
      ((map_continuous f).tendsto 0).comp (hl.tendsto_commutator a)
  have hmul : ∀ y ∈ I.map f, Tendsto (fun e => f e * y) l (𝓝 y) := by
    intro y hy
    induction hy using TwoSidedIdeal.span_induction with
    | mem _ h =>
      rcases h with ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
      simpa only [Function.comp_def, map_mul] using
        ((map_continuous f).tendsto x).comp (hl.tendsto_mul_right hx)
    | zero =>
      simp only [mul_zero]
      exact tendsto_const_nhds
    | add _ _ _ _ hy hz => simpa only [mul_add] using hy.add hz
    | neg _ _ hy => simpa only [mul_neg] using hy.neg
    | left_absorb b y _ hy =>
      have h1 : Tendsto (fun e => (f e * b - b * f e) * y + b * (f e * y)) l (𝓝 (0 * y + b * y)) :=
        ((hcomm b).mul_const y).add (hy.const_mul b)
      simpa only [zero_mul, zero_add, sub_mul, mul_assoc, sub_add_cancel] using h1
    | right_absorb b _ _ hy => simpa only [mul_assoc] using hy.mul_const b
  exact .of_tendsto_mul_right
    (eventually_map.mpr <| hl.eventually_mem.mono fun e he =>
      TwoSidedIdeal.subset_span ⟨e, he, rfl⟩)
    (eventually_map.mpr <| hl.eventually_nonneg.mono fun _ hx => map_nonneg f hx)
    (eventually_map.mpr <| hl.eventually_norm.mono fun e he =>
      (NonUnitalStarAlgHom.norm_apply_le f e).trans he)
    (fun y hy => tendsto_map'_iff.mpr (hmul y hy))
    (fun b => tendsto_map'_iff.mpr (hcomm b))

end Map

section CanonicalFilter

variable {A : Type*} [NonUnitalCStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A]

/-- Finite-set quasicentral approximation neighborhood of a two-sided ideal `I`. -/
private def quasicentralSet (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) (G : Finset I) (F : Finset A) (ε : ℝ) : Set A :=
  {e : A | e ∈ I ∧ 0 ≤ e ∧ ‖e‖ ≤ 1 ∧
    (∀ x ∈ G, ‖e * (x : A) - x‖ < ε ∧ ‖(x : A) * e - x‖ < ε) ∧
    (∀ a ∈ F, ‖e * a - a * e‖ < ε)}

/-- Explicit set-builder form of `quasicentralSet`. -/
private theorem quasicentralSet_eq (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) (G : Finset I) (F : Finset A) (ε : ℝ) :
    quasicentralSet I G F ε =
      {e : A | e ∈ I ∧ 0 ≤ e ∧ ‖e‖ ≤ 1 ∧
        (∀ x ∈ G, ‖e * (x : A) - x‖ < ε ∧ ‖(x : A) * e - x‖ < ε) ∧
        (∀ a ∈ F, ‖e * a - a * e‖ < ε)} := rfl

private theorem quasicentralSet_anti (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) {G₁ G₂ : Finset I} (hG : G₁ ⊆ G₂)
    {F₁ F₂ : Finset A} (hF : F₁ ⊆ F₂) {ε₁ ε₂ : ℝ} (hε : ε₂ ≤ ε₁) :
    quasicentralSet I G₂ F₂ ε₂ ⊆ quasicentralSet I G₁ F₁ ε₁ :=
  fun _ ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, h5⟩ => ⟨h1, h2, h3,
    fun x hx => ⟨(h4 x (hG hx)).1.trans_le hε, (h4 x (hG hx)).2.trans_le hε⟩,
    fun a ha => (h5 a (hF ha)).trans_le hε⟩

/-- The canonical filter generated by the finite-set quasicentral approximation neighborhoods of a
two-sided ideal `I` of `A` (see `TwoSidedIdeal.hasBasis_quasicentralApproximateUnit`). Whenever `I`
admits a quasicentral approximate unit—in particular, when `I` is closed in a star-ordered
C⋆-algebra (`TwoSidedIdeal.isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_quasicentralApproximateUnit`)—this is the
coarsest quasicentral approximate unit of `I`. -/
def quasicentralApproximateUnit (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) : Filter A :=
  ⨅ (p : Finset I × Finset A × ℝ) (_ : 0 < p.2.2), 𝓟 (quasicentralSet I p.1 p.2.1 p.2.2)

/-- Explicit filter basis of `I.quasicentralApproximateUnit` indexed by `(G, F, ε)` with `G` a
finite subset of `I`, `F` a finite subset of `A`, and `0 < ε`. -/
theorem hasBasis_quasicentralApproximateUnit (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) :
    I.quasicentralApproximateUnit.HasBasis (fun p : Finset I × Finset A × ℝ => 0 < p.2.2)
      (fun p => {e : A | e ∈ I ∧ 0 ≤ e ∧ ‖e‖ ≤ 1 ∧
        (∀ x ∈ p.1, ‖e * (x : A) - x‖ < p.2.2 ∧ ‖(x : A) * e - x‖ < p.2.2) ∧
        (∀ a ∈ p.2.1, ‖e * a - a * e‖ < p.2.2)}) := by
  classical
  simp_rw [← quasicentralSet_eq]
  refine hasBasis_biInf_principal' ?_ ⟨(∅, ∅, 1), zero_lt_one⟩
  rintro ⟨G₁, F₁, ε₁⟩ hε₁ ⟨G₂, F₂, ε₂⟩ hε₂
  refine ⟨(G₁ ∪ G₂, F₁ ∪ F₂, min ε₁ ε₂), lt_min hε₁ hε₂,
    quasicentralSet_anti I Finset.subset_union_left Finset.subset_union_left (min_le_left _ _),
    quasicentralSet_anti I Finset.subset_union_right Finset.subset_union_right (min_le_right _ _)⟩

/-- Membership in `I.quasicentralApproximateUnit` in terms of finite subsets `G ⊆ I`, `F ⊆ A`, and
`ε > 0`. -/
theorem mem_quasicentralApproximateUnit_iff {I : TwoSidedIdeal A} {s : Set A} :
    s ∈ I.quasicentralApproximateUnit ↔
      ∃ G : Finset I, ∃ F : Finset A, ∃ ε > 0,
        {e : A | e ∈ I ∧ 0 ≤ e ∧ ‖e‖ ≤ 1 ∧
          (∀ x ∈ G, ‖e * (x : A) - x‖ < ε ∧ ‖(x : A) * e - x‖ < ε) ∧
          (∀ a ∈ F, ‖e * a - a * e‖ < ε)} ⊆ s := by
  rw [(hasBasis_quasicentralApproximateUnit I).mem_iff]
  simp only [Prod.exists]

/-- Pushing `I.quasicentralApproximateUnit.comap ((↑) : I → A)` forward to `A` recovers
`I.quasicentralApproximateUnit`. -/
@[simp]
theorem map_coe_comap_coe_quasicentralApproximateUnit (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) :
    (I.quasicentralApproximateUnit.comap ((↑) : I → A)).map ((↑) : I → A) =
      I.quasicentralApproximateUnit := by
  refine map_comap_of_mem (mem_quasicentralApproximateUnit_iff.mpr ?_)
  exact ⟨∅, ∅, 1, zero_lt_one, fun e h => ⟨⟨e, h.1⟩, rfl⟩⟩

/-- Universal property of `I.quasicentralApproximateUnit`: a filter `l` is finer than
`I.quasicentralApproximateUnit` precisely when it satisfies all eventual bounds and convergence
clauses of a quasicentral approximate unit. -/
theorem le_quasicentralApproximateUnit_iff {I : TwoSidedIdeal A} {l : Filter A} :
    l ≤ I.quasicentralApproximateUnit ↔
      (∀ᶠ e in l, e ∈ I ∧ 0 ≤ e ∧ ‖e‖ ≤ 1) ∧
        (∀ x ∈ I, Tendsto (· * x) l (𝓝 x)) ∧
        (∀ x ∈ I, Tendsto (x * ·) l (𝓝 x)) ∧
        (∀ a : A, Tendsto (fun e => e * a - a * e) l (𝓝 0)) := by
  rw [(hasBasis_quasicentralApproximateUnit I).ge_iff]
  constructor
  · intro h
    refine ⟨?_, fun x hx => Metric.tendsto_nhds.mpr fun ε hε => ?_,
      fun x hx => Metric.tendsto_nhds.mpr fun ε hε => ?_,
      fun a => Metric.tendsto_nhds.mpr fun ε hε => ?_⟩
    · exact mem_of_superset (h (∅, ∅, 1) zero_lt_one) fun _ ⟨h1, h2, h3, _, _⟩ => ⟨h1, h2, h3⟩
    · exact mem_of_superset (h ({⟨x, hx⟩}, ∅, ε) hε) fun e ⟨_, _, _, hG, _⟩ => by
        simpa only [dist_eq_norm] using! (hG ⟨x, hx⟩ (Finset.mem_singleton_self _)).1
    · exact mem_of_superset (h ({⟨x, hx⟩}, ∅, ε) hε) fun e ⟨_, _, _, hG, _⟩ => by
        simpa only [dist_eq_norm] using! (hG ⟨x, hx⟩ (Finset.mem_singleton_self _)).2
    · exact mem_of_superset (h (∅, {a}, ε) hε) fun e ⟨_, _, _, _, hF⟩ => by
        simpa only [dist_zero_right] using! hF a (Finset.mem_singleton_self a)
  · rintro ⟨hmem, hmr, hml, hc⟩ ⟨G, F, ε⟩ (hε : 0 < ε)
    have hG : ∀ᶠ e in l, ∀ x ∈ G, ‖e * (x : A) - x‖ < ε ∧ ‖(x : A) * e - x‖ < ε :=
      G.eventually_all.mpr fun x _ =>
        ((Metric.tendsto_nhds.mp (hmr x x.2) ε hε).and
          (Metric.tendsto_nhds.mp (hml x x.2) ε hε)).mono fun _ ⟨h1, h2⟩ => by
          simpa only [dist_eq_norm] using And.intro h1 h2
    have hF : ∀ᶠ e in l, ∀ a ∈ F, ‖e * a - a * e‖ < ε :=
      F.eventually_all.mpr fun a _ =>
        (Metric.tendsto_nhds.mp (hc a) ε hε).mono fun _ ha => by
          simpa only [dist_zero_right] using ha
    exact (hmem.and (hG.and hF)).mono fun _ ⟨⟨h1, h2, h3⟩, h4, h5⟩ => ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4, h5⟩

/-- Every quasicentral approximate unit of `I` is finer than `I.quasicentralApproximateUnit`: a
filter `l` is a quasicentral approximate unit of `I` if and only if `l` is proper (`l.NeBot`) and
`l ≤ I.quasicentralApproximateUnit` (so `I.quasicentralApproximateUnit` is the largest quasicentral
approximate unit of `I` whenever one exists). -/
theorem isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_neBot_and_le {I : TwoSidedIdeal A} {l : Filter A} :
    I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l ↔ l.NeBot ∧ l ≤ I.quasicentralApproximateUnit := by
  rw [isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff, le_quasicentralApproximateUnit_iff]

/-- When `l` is proper, `I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l` is equivalent to
`l ≤ I.quasicentralApproximateUnit`. -/
theorem isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_le {I : TwoSidedIdeal A} {l : Filter A} [hl : l.NeBot] :
    I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l ↔ l ≤ I.quasicentralApproximateUnit := by
  simp [isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_neBot_and_le, hl]

/-- `I` admits a quasicentral approximate unit filter iff `I.quasicentralApproximateUnit` is
proper. -/
theorem exists_isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_neBot (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) :
    (∃ l : Filter A, I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) ↔ I.quasicentralApproximateUnit.NeBot :=
  ⟨fun ⟨_, hl⟩ => (isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_neBot_and_le.mp hl).1.mono
    (isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_neBot_and_le.mp hl).2,
   fun h => ⟨I.quasicentralApproximateUnit,
    isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_neBot_and_le.mpr ⟨h, le_rfl⟩⟩⟩

/-- Finite-set criterion: `I` admits a quasicentral approximate unit iff every finite subset `G` of
`I` and finite subset `F` of `A` admit a single positive contraction in `I` fixing `G` and
commuting with `F` up to `ε`. -/
theorem exists_isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_forall_finset (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) :
    (∃ l : Filter A, I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) ↔
      ∀ G : Finset I, ∀ F : Finset A, ∀ ε > 0,
        ∃ e ∈ I, 0 ≤ e ∧ ‖e‖ ≤ 1 ∧
          (∀ x ∈ G, ‖e * (x : A) - x‖ < ε ∧ ‖(x : A) * e - x‖ < ε) ∧
          (∀ a ∈ F, ‖e * a - a * e‖ < ε) := by
  rw [exists_isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_neBot,
    (hasBasis_quasicentralApproximateUnit I).neBot_iff]
  simp only [Prod.forall, Set.Nonempty, Set.mem_ofPred_eq]

/-- The canonical quasicentral approximate unit of the zero ideal `⊥` is `pure 0`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quasicentralApproximateUnit_bot :
    (⊥ : TwoSidedIdeal A).quasicentralApproximateUnit = pure 0 := by
  have hpure : pure 0 ≤ (⊥ : TwoSidedIdeal A).quasicentralApproximateUnit :=
    (isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_neBot_and_le.mp
      IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit.bot_pure_zero).2
  have hne : (⊥ : TwoSidedIdeal A).quasicentralApproximateUnit.NeBot :=
    (pure_neBot (a := (0 : A))).mono hpure
  exact isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_bot_iff.mp
    (isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_neBot_and_le.mpr ⟨hne, le_rfl⟩)

end CanonicalFilter

end TwoSidedIdeal

namespace TauCeti.CStarAlgebra

/-- C⋆-identity estimate on the squared norm of a finite sum in a C⋆-ring: if every term `d i`
(`i ∈ s`) has norm at most `C` and every off-diagonal product `star (d i) * d j` (`i ≠ j`) has norm
at most `η` (`0 ≤ η`), then `‖∑ i ∈ s, d i‖ ^ 2 ≤ s.card * C ^ 2 + s.card ^ 2 * η`. -/
theorem norm_sum_sq_le {A ι : Type*} [NonUnitalNormedRing A] [StarRing A] [CStarRing A]
    {s : Finset ι} {d : ι → A} {C η : ℝ} (hη : 0 ≤ η)
    (hd : ∀ i ∈ s, ‖d i‖ ≤ C)
    (hoff : ∀ i ∈ s, ∀ j ∈ s, i ≠ j → ‖star (d i) * d j‖ ≤ η) :
    ‖∑ i ∈ s, d i‖ ^ 2 ≤ (s.card : ℝ) * C ^ 2 + (s.card : ℝ) ^ 2 * η := by
  classical
  have hterm : ∀ i ∈ s, ∀ j ∈ s,
      ‖star (d i) * d j‖ ≤ (if i = j then C ^ 2 else 0) + η := by
    intro i hi j hj
    split_ifs with hij
    · subst hij
      rw [CStarRing.norm_star_mul_self, ← sq]
      exact (pow_le_pow_left₀ (norm_nonneg _) (hd i hi) 2).trans (le_add_of_nonneg_right hη)
    · simpa only [zero_add] using hoff i hi j hj hij
  calc ‖∑ i ∈ s, d i‖ ^ 2
      = ‖∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, star (d i) * d j‖ := by
        rw [sq, ← CStarRing.norm_star_mul_self, star_sum, Finset.sum_mul]
        simp_rw [Finset.mul_sum]
    _ ≤ ∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, ‖star (d i) * d j‖ :=
        (norm_sum_le _ _).trans (Finset.sum_le_sum fun _ _ => norm_sum_le _ _)
    _ ≤ ∑ i ∈ s, ∑ j ∈ s, ((if i = j then C ^ 2 else 0) + η) :=
        Finset.sum_le_sum fun i hi => Finset.sum_le_sum fun j hj => hterm i hi j hj
    _ = (s.card : ℝ) * C ^ 2 + (s.card : ℝ) ^ 2 * η := by
        simp only [Finset.sum_add_distrib, Finset.sum_ite_eq, Finset.sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul]
        rw [Finset.sum_ite_of_true fun _ hx => hx, Finset.sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul]
        ring

end TauCeti.CStarAlgebra

namespace TwoSidedIdeal

section Existence

variable {A : Type*} [NonUnitalCStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A] [StarOrderedRing A]

/-- Single inductive step along `CStarAlgebra.approximateUnit`: given `u_0, …, u_{n-1} ∈ I`, find a
positive contraction `v ∈ I` that approximates `G` within `ε` and satisfies
`‖star (u_i * a - a * u_i) * (v * a - a * v)‖ ≤ δ * (‖a‖ + 1)` for all `i < n` and `a ∈ F`. -/
private theorem exists_next_quasicentral_step (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) [IsClosed (I : Set A)]
    {n : ℕ} {u : ℕ → A} (hu : ∀ i < n, u i ∈ I)
    (G : Finset I) (F : Finset A) {ε δ : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) (hδ : 0 < δ) :
    ∃ v ∈ I, 0 ≤ v ∧ ‖v‖ ≤ 1 ∧
      (∀ x ∈ G, ‖v * (x : A) - x‖ < ε ∧ ‖(x : A) * v - x‖ < ε) ∧
      (∀ i < n, ∀ a ∈ F,
        ‖star (u i * a - a * u i) * (v * a - a * v)‖ ≤ δ * (‖a‖ + 1)) := by
  let S := I.toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra
  let l₀ : Filter S := CStarAlgebra.approximateUnit S
  have hl₀ : l₀.IsIncreasingApproximateUnit := CStarAlgebra.increasingApproximateUnit S
  have := hl₀.neBot
  have hmul_l {y : A} (hy : y ∈ I) : Tendsto (fun v : S => y * (v : A)) l₀ (𝓝 y) :=
    (continuous_subtype_val.tendsto ⟨y, I.mem_toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra.mpr hy⟩).comp
      (hl₀.tendsto_mul_left ⟨y, I.mem_toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra.mpr hy⟩)
  have hmul_r {y : A} (hy : y ∈ I) : Tendsto (fun v : S => (v : A) * y) l₀ (𝓝 y) :=
    (continuous_subtype_val.tendsto ⟨y, I.mem_toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra.mpr hy⟩).comp
      (hl₀.tendsto_mul_right ⟨y, I.mem_toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra.mpr hy⟩)
  have hG : ∀ᶠ v : S in l₀, ∀ x ∈ G,
      ‖(v : A) * (x : A) - x‖ < ε ∧ ‖(x : A) * (v : A) - x‖ < ε :=
    G.eventually_all.mpr fun x _ =>
      ((Metric.tendsto_nhds.mp (hmul_r x.2) ε hε).and
        (Metric.tendsto_nhds.mp (hmul_l x.2) ε hε)).mono fun v ⟨hr, hl⟩ =>
        ⟨by simpa only [dist_eq_norm] using hr, by simpa only [dist_eq_norm] using hl⟩
  have hF : ∀ᶠ v : S in l₀, ∀ i ∈ Finset.range n, ∀ a ∈ F,
      ‖star (u i * a - a * u i) * ((v : A) * a - a * (v : A))‖ ≤ δ * (‖a‖ + 1) := by
    refine (Finset.range n).eventually_all.mpr fun i hi => F.eventually_all.mpr fun a _ => ?_
    have hui : u i ∈ I := hu i (Finset.mem_range.mp hi)
    have hsd : star (u i * a - a * u i) ∈ I :=
      I.star_mem_of_isClosed (I.sub_mem (I.mul_mem_right _ _ hui) (I.mul_mem_left _ _ hui))
    filter_upwards [Metric.tendsto_nhds.mp (hmul_l hsd) δ hδ,
      Metric.tendsto_nhds.mp (hmul_l (I.mul_mem_right _ _ hsd)) δ hδ] with v hv₁ hv₂
    have h1 : ‖star (u i * a - a * u i) * (v : A) - star (u i * a - a * u i)‖ ≤ δ := by
      simpa only [dist_eq_norm] using hv₁.le
    have h2 : ‖star (u i * a - a * u i) * a * (v : A) - star (u i * a - a * u i) * a‖ ≤ δ := by
      simpa only [dist_eq_norm] using hv₂.le
    have hid : star (u i * a - a * u i) * ((v : A) * a - a * (v : A)) =
        (star (u i * a - a * u i) * (v : A) - star (u i * a - a * u i)) * a -
          (star (u i * a - a * u i) * a * (v : A) - star (u i * a - a * u i) * a) := by
      noncomm_ring
    rw [hid]
    calc ‖_ - _‖ ≤ ‖star (u i * a - a * u i) * (v : A) - star (u i * a - a * u i)‖ * ‖a‖ +
            ‖star (u i * a - a * u i) * a * (v : A) - star (u i * a - a * u i) * a‖ :=
          (norm_sub_le _ _).trans (add_le_add (norm_mul_le _ _) le_rfl)
      _ ≤ δ * ‖a‖ + δ := add_le_add (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right h1 (norm_nonneg a)) h2
      _ = δ * (‖a‖ + 1) := by ring
  obtain ⟨v, ⟨hv₀, hv₁⟩, hvG, hvF⟩ :=
    ((hl₀.eventually_nonneg.and hl₀.eventually_norm).and (hG.and hF)).exists
  exact ⟨v.1, I.mem_toNonUnitalStarSubalgebra.mp v.2, Subtype.coe_le_coe.mpr hv₀,
    by rwa [AddSubgroupClass.coe_norm] at hv₁, hvG,
    fun i hi a ha => hvF i (Finset.mem_range.mpr hi) a ha⟩

/-- Iterated choice of `n` positive contractions `u_0, …, u_{n-1} ∈ I` with pairwise controlled
commutator inner products. -/
private theorem exists_tuple_quasicentral (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) [IsClosed (I : Set A)]
    (G : Finset I) (F : Finset A) {ε δ : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) (hδ : 0 < δ) (n : ℕ) :
    ∃ u : ℕ → A,
      (∀ k < n, u k ∈ I ∧ 0 ≤ u k ∧ ‖u k‖ ≤ 1 ∧
        (∀ x ∈ G, ‖u k * (x : A) - x‖ < ε ∧ ‖(x : A) * u k - x‖ < ε)) ∧
      (∀ i j, i < j → j < n → ∀ a ∈ F,
        ‖star (u i * a - a * u i) * (u j * a - a * u j)‖ ≤ δ * (‖a‖ + 1)) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => exact ⟨fun _ => 0, by simp, by simp⟩
  | succ n ih =>
    classical
    obtain ⟨u, hu, hoff⟩ := ih
    obtain ⟨v, hvI, hv₀, hv₁, hvG, hvF⟩ :=
      exists_next_quasicentral_step I (fun i hi => (hu i hi).1) G F hε hδ
    refine ⟨Function.update u n v, fun k hk => ?_, fun i j hij hjn a ha => ?_⟩
    · rcases Nat.lt_succ_iff_lt_or_eq.mp hk with hkn | rfl
      · simpa only [Function.update_of_ne hkn.ne] using hu k hkn
      · simpa only [Function.update_self] using ⟨hvI, hv₀, hv₁, hvG⟩
    · rcases Nat.lt_succ_iff_lt_or_eq.mp hjn with hjn' | rfl
      · rw [Function.update_of_ne (hij.trans hjn').ne, Function.update_of_ne hjn'.ne]
        exact hoff i j hij hjn' a ha
      · rw [Function.update_of_ne hij.ne, Function.update_self]
        exact hvF i hij a ha

/-- Convexity properties of the Cesàro average `(n : ℝ)⁻¹ • ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, u k`: it remains
a positive contraction in `I` and preserves strict `ε`-approximation on `G`. -/
private theorem cesaro_mem_and_mul_lt (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) [IsClosed (I : Set A)]
    {G : Finset I} {ε : ℝ} {n : ℕ} (hn_pos : 0 < n) {u : ℕ → A}
    (hu : ∀ k < n, u k ∈ I ∧ 0 ≤ u k ∧ ‖u k‖ ≤ 1 ∧
      (∀ x ∈ G, ‖u k * (x : A) - x‖ < ε ∧ ‖(x : A) * u k - x‖ < ε)) :
    let e : A := (n : ℝ)⁻¹ • ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, u k
    e ∈ I ∧ 0 ≤ e ∧ ‖e‖ ≤ 1 ∧
      ∀ x ∈ G, ‖e * (x : A) - x‖ < ε ∧ ‖(x : A) * e - x‖ < ε := by
  intro e
  have hnR : (0 : ℝ) < n := by positivity
  have heI : e ∈ I := by
    let c : ℝ := (n : ℝ)⁻¹
    have hec : e = (c : ℂ) • ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, u k :=
      (Complex.coe_smul c (∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, u k)).symm
    rw [hec]
    exact I.smul_mem_of_isClosed _ <| I.mem_toSubmodule.mp <|
      Submodule.sum_mem I.toSubmodule fun k hk =>
        I.mem_toSubmodule.mpr (hu k (Finset.mem_range.mp hk)).1
  have he₀ : 0 ≤ e := smul_nonneg (by positivity)
    (Finset.sum_nonneg fun k hk => (hu k (Finset.mem_range.mp hk)).2.1)
  have he₁ : ‖e‖ ≤ 1 := by
    rw [norm_smul, Real.norm_of_nonneg (by positivity)]
    calc (n : ℝ)⁻¹ * ‖∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, u k‖
        ≤ (n : ℝ)⁻¹ * ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, ‖u k‖ :=
          mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (norm_sum_le _ _) (by positivity)
      _ ≤ (n : ℝ)⁻¹ * ∑ _k ∈ Finset.range n, (1 : ℝ) :=
          mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left
            (Finset.sum_le_sum fun k hk => (hu k (Finset.mem_range.mp hk)).2.2.1) (by positivity)
      _ = 1 := by simp [hnR.ne']
  have havg (f : ℕ → A) (y : A) (hf : ∀ k < n, ‖f k - y‖ < ε) :
      ‖((n : ℝ)⁻¹ • ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, f k) - y‖ < ε := by
    have hsub : ((n : ℝ)⁻¹ • ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, f k) - y =
        (n : ℝ)⁻¹ • ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, (f k - y) := by
      simp [Finset.sum_sub_distrib, smul_sub, ← Nat.cast_smul_eq_nsmul ℝ, smul_smul, hnR.ne']
    rw [hsub, norm_smul, Real.norm_of_nonneg (by positivity)]
    calc (n : ℝ)⁻¹ * ‖∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, (f k - y)‖
        ≤ (n : ℝ)⁻¹ * ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, ‖f k - y‖ :=
          mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (norm_sum_le _ _) (by positivity)
      _ < (n : ℝ)⁻¹ * ∑ _k ∈ Finset.range n, ε := mul_lt_mul_of_pos_left
          (Finset.sum_lt_sum_of_nonempty ⟨0, Finset.mem_range.mpr hn_pos⟩
            fun k hk => hf k (Finset.mem_range.mp hk)) (by positivity)
      _ = ε := by simp [hnR.ne']
  refine ⟨heI, he₀, he₁, fun x hx => ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩
  · simpa only [e, smul_mul_assoc, Finset.sum_mul] using
      havg (fun k => u k * (x : A)) x (fun k hk => ((hu k hk).2.2.2 x hx).1)
  · simpa only [e, mul_smul_comm, Finset.mul_sum] using
      havg (fun k => (x : A) * u k) x (fun k hk => ((hu k hk).2.2.2 x hx).2)

/-- **Finite-set Arveson–Akemann–Pedersen theorem.** For every closed two-sided ideal `I` of a
C⋆-algebra `A`, finite subsets `G ⊆ I` and `F ⊆ A`, and `ε > 0`, there exists a positive
contraction `e ∈ I` such that `‖e * x - x‖ < ε` and `‖x * e - x‖ < ε` for all `x ∈ G`, and
`‖e * a - a * e‖ < ε` for all `a ∈ F`. -/
theorem exists_mem_nonneg_norm_le_one_norm_mul_sub_lt_norm_commutator_lt
    (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) [IsClosed (I : Set A)]
    (G : Finset I) (F : Finset A) {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) :
    ∃ e ∈ I, 0 ≤ e ∧ ‖e‖ ≤ 1 ∧
      (∀ x ∈ G, ‖e * (x : A) - x‖ < ε ∧ ‖(x : A) * e - x‖ < ε) ∧
      (∀ a ∈ F, ‖e * a - a * e‖ < ε) := by
  let M : ℝ := ∑ a ∈ F, ‖a‖ + 1
  have hM : 0 < M := add_pos_of_nonneg_of_pos (Finset.sum_nonneg fun b _ => norm_nonneg b) one_pos
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := exists_nat_gt (8 * M ^ 2 / ε ^ 2)
  let n : ℕ := m + 1
  have hn_pos : 0 < n := Nat.succ_pos m
  have hnR : (0 : ℝ) < n := by positivity
  let δ : ℝ := ε ^ 2 / (4 * (M + 1))
  obtain ⟨u, hu, hoff⟩ := exists_tuple_quasicentral I G F hε (δ := δ) (by positivity) n
  let e : A := (n : ℝ)⁻¹ • ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, u k
  obtain ⟨heI, he₀, he₁, heG⟩ := cesaro_mem_and_mul_lt I hn_pos hu
  refine ⟨e, heI, he₀, he₁, heG, fun a ha => ?_⟩
  have haM : ‖a‖ ≤ M :=
    (Finset.single_le_sum (fun b _ => norm_nonneg b) ha).trans (le_add_of_nonneg_right zero_le_one)
  have hcomm : e * a - a * e = (n : ℝ)⁻¹ • ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, (u k * a - a * u k) := by
    simp [e, Finset.sum_sub_distrib, Finset.sum_mul, Finset.mul_sum, smul_sub, smul_mul_assoc,
      mul_smul_comm]
  have hoff_lt {i j : ℕ} (hij : i < j) (hjn : j < n) :
      ‖star (u i * a - a * u i) * (u j * a - a * u j)‖ ≤ ε ^ 2 / 4 :=
    (hoff i j hij hjn a ha).trans <| by
      calc δ * (‖a‖ + 1) ≤ δ * (M + 1) := by gcongr
        _ = ε ^ 2 / 4 := by dsimp [δ]; field_simp
  have hsq := TauCeti.CStarAlgebra.norm_sum_sq_le (s := Finset.range n)
    (d := fun k => u k * a - a * u k) (C := 2 * ‖a‖) (η := ε ^ 2 / 4) (by positivity)
    (fun k hk => norm_commutator_le_two_mul_norm (hu k (Finset.mem_range.mp hk)).2.2.1 a)
    (fun i hi j hj hij => by
      rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne hij with h | h
      · exact hoff_lt h (Finset.mem_range.mp hj)
      · rw [← norm_star, star_mul, star_star]
        exact hoff_lt h (Finset.mem_range.mp hi))
  rw [Finset.card_range] at hsq
  have hterm1 : 4 * ‖a‖ ^ 2 / (n : ℝ) < ε ^ 2 / 2 := by
    have hmn : 8 * M ^ 2 / ε ^ 2 < (n : ℝ) := hm.trans (by exact_mod_cast Nat.lt_succ_self m)
    rw [div_lt_iff₀ (by positivity)] at hmn
    rw [div_lt_div_iff₀ hnR two_pos]
    have ha2 : ‖a‖ ^ 2 ≤ M ^ 2 := pow_le_pow_left₀ (norm_nonneg a) haM 2
    nlinarith
  have hlt : ‖e * a - a * e‖ ^ 2 < ε ^ 2 := by
    rw [hcomm, norm_smul, Real.norm_of_nonneg (by positivity), mul_pow]
    calc ((n : ℝ)⁻¹) ^ 2 * ‖∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, (u k * a - a * u k)‖ ^ 2
        ≤ ((n : ℝ)⁻¹) ^ 2 * ((n : ℝ) * (2 * ‖a‖) ^ 2 + (n : ℝ) ^ 2 * (ε ^ 2 / 4)) :=
          mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left hsq (by positivity)
      _ = 4 * ‖a‖ ^ 2 / (n : ℝ) + ε ^ 2 / 4 := by field_simp; ring
      _ < ε ^ 2 / 2 + ε ^ 2 / 2 := add_lt_add hterm1
          (div_lt_div_of_pos_left (sq_pos_of_pos hε) two_pos (by norm_num))
      _ = ε ^ 2 := add_halves _
  exact lt_of_pow_lt_pow_left₀ 2 hε.le hlt

/-- Finite-set Arveson theorem for a subset `G : Finset A` contained in `I`. -/
theorem exists_mem_nonneg_norm_le_one_norm_mul_sub_lt_norm_commutator_lt_of_subset
    (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) [IsClosed (I : Set A)]
    {G : Finset A} (hGI : (G : Set A) ⊆ I) (F : Finset A) {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) :
    ∃ e ∈ I, 0 ≤ e ∧ ‖e‖ ≤ 1 ∧
      (∀ x ∈ G, ‖e * x - x‖ < ε ∧ ‖x * e - x‖ < ε) ∧
      (∀ a ∈ F, ‖e * a - a * e‖ < ε) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨e, heI, he₀, he₁, heG, heF⟩ :=
    I.exists_mem_nonneg_norm_le_one_norm_mul_sub_lt_norm_commutator_lt (G.subtype (· ∈ I)) F hε
  exact ⟨e, heI, he₀, he₁, fun x hx => heG ⟨x, hGI hx⟩ (Finset.mem_subtype.mpr hx), heF⟩

/-- For every closed two-sided ideal `I` of a C⋆-algebra `A`, the canonical filter
`I.quasicentralApproximateUnit` is proper (`NeBot`). -/
instance quasicentralApproximateUnit_neBot (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) [IsClosed (I : Set A)] :
    I.quasicentralApproximateUnit.NeBot :=
  (hasBasis_quasicentralApproximateUnit I).neBot_iff.mpr fun {p} hε =>
    I.exists_mem_nonneg_norm_le_one_norm_mul_sub_lt_norm_commutator_lt p.1 p.2.1 hε

/-- **Arveson's theorem.** For every closed two-sided ideal `I` of a C⋆-algebra `A`,
`I.quasicentralApproximateUnit` is a quasicentral approximate unit of `I` in `A`. -/
theorem isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_quasicentralApproximateUnit (I : TwoSidedIdeal A)
    [IsClosed (I : Set A)] :
    I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit I.quasicentralApproximateUnit :=
  isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_neBot_and_le.mpr ⟨inferInstance, le_rfl⟩

/-- **Arveson's theorem** (existential form): every closed two-sided ideal `I` of a C⋆-algebra `A`
admits a positive contractive approximate unit that is quasicentral in `A`. -/
theorem exists_isQuasicentralApproximateUnit (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) [IsClosed (I : Set A)] :
    ∃ l : Filter A, I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l :=
  ⟨I.quasicentralApproximateUnit, I.isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_quasicentralApproximateUnit⟩

end Existence

section Sequential

variable {A : Type*} [NonUnitalCStarAlgebra A] [PartialOrder A] [TopologicalSpace.SeparableSpace A]

/-- On a separable C⋆-algebra `A`, a two-sided ideal `I` admits a quasicentral approximate unit
filter if and only if it admits a sequential quasicentral approximate unit `u : ℕ → A` with
`u n ∈ I`, `0 ≤ u n`, and `‖u n‖ ≤ 1` for every `n`. -/
theorem exists_isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_exists_seq (I : TwoSidedIdeal A) :
    (∃ l : Filter A, I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit l) ↔
      ∃ u : ℕ → A, (∀ n, u n ∈ I ∧ 0 ≤ u n ∧ ‖u n‖ ≤ 1) ∧
        I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit (atTop.map u) := by
  refine ⟨fun h => ?_, fun ⟨u, _, hu⟩ => ⟨atTop.map u, hu⟩⟩
  classical
  have hfin := (exists_isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_forall_finset I).mp h
  have : TopologicalSpace.SeparableSpace I :=
    (TopologicalSpace.IsSeparable.of_separableSpace (I : Set A)).separableSpace
  have : Nonempty I := ⟨⟨0, I.zero_mem⟩⟩
  let dI := TopologicalSpace.denseSeq I
  let dA := TopologicalSpace.denseSeq A
  choose u huI hu₀ hu₁ huG huF using fun n : ℕ =>
    hfin ((Finset.range n).image dI) ((Finset.range n).image dA) (1 / ((n : ℝ) + 1)) (by positivity)
  have hsI : (I : Set A) ⊆ closure (Set.range fun k => (dI k : A)) := by
    intro x hx
    have hx' : (⟨x, hx⟩ : I) ∈ closure (Set.range dI) :=
      TopologicalSpace.denseRange_denseSeq I ⟨x, hx⟩
    have himg := image_closure_subset_closure_image continuous_subtype_val ⟨⟨x, hx⟩, hx', rfl⟩
    rwa [← Set.range_comp] at himg
  refine ⟨u, fun n => ⟨huI n, hu₀ n, hu₁ n⟩, ?_⟩
  have : (atTop.map u).NeBot := atTop_neBot.map u
  refine IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit.of_tendsto_mul_right_of_dense
    (eventually_map.mpr (Eventually.of_forall huI))
    (eventually_map.mpr (Eventually.of_forall hu₀))
    (eventually_map.mpr (Eventually.of_forall hu₁))
    hsI (TopologicalSpace.denseRange_denseSeq A) ?_ ?_
  · rintro _ ⟨k, rfl⟩
    rw [tendsto_map'_iff, Metric.tendsto_nhds]
    intro ε hε
    filter_upwards [(tendsto_one_div_add_atTop_nhds_zero_nat (𝕜 := ℝ)).eventually (gt_mem_nhds hε),
      eventually_gt_atTop k] with n hn hkn
    simpa only [Function.comp_def, dist_eq_norm] using
      ((huG n (dI k) (Finset.mem_image.mpr ⟨k, Finset.mem_range.mpr hkn, rfl⟩)).1).trans hn
  · rintro _ ⟨k, rfl⟩
    rw [tendsto_map'_iff, Metric.tendsto_nhds]
    intro ε hε
    filter_upwards [(tendsto_one_div_add_atTop_nhds_zero_nat (𝕜 := ℝ)).eventually (gt_mem_nhds hε),
      eventually_gt_atTop k] with n hn hkn
    simpa only [Function.comp_def, dist_zero_right] using
      (huF n (dA k) (Finset.mem_image.mpr ⟨k, Finset.mem_range.mpr hkn, rfl⟩)).trans hn

/-- Every closed two-sided ideal `I` of a separable C⋆-algebra `A` admits a sequential
quasicentral approximate unit `u : ℕ → A` in the nonnegative closed unit ball of `I`. -/
theorem exists_seq_isQuasicentralApproximateUnit [StarOrderedRing A] (I : TwoSidedIdeal A)
    [IsClosed (I : Set A)] :
    ∃ u : ℕ → A, (∀ n, u n ∈ I ∧ 0 ≤ u n ∧ ‖u n‖ ≤ 1) ∧
      I.IsQuasicentralApproximateUnit (atTop.map u) :=
  (exists_isQuasicentralApproximateUnit_iff_exists_seq I).mp
    (exists_isQuasicentralApproximateUnit I)

end Sequential

end TwoSidedIdeal
